Why not await?
legacy_network_call is a regular function (def). Awaiting it doesn't make it non-blocking; it just stops the loop until it finishes.

The GIL?
Standard I/O operations (like requests) release the GIL, allowing threads to run concurrently for network tasks.

CPU vs I/O?
Use ProcessPoolExecutor for CPU-bound tasks to bypass the GIL and utilize multiple CPU cores.

Modernization?
httpx or aiohttp. These libraries are designed for async/await and don't require an executor.
